    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-03-30T18:48:05Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "What setup do you have? If it is [this basic recommended one](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d0464ced00abfd9bbed196fa36ccf3b1691c6b2c/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L379-L390) with 'rafamadriz/friendly-snippets' installed then making react snippets to work in tsx/jsx files needs more setup. This is both due to how 'friendly-snippets' organize their snippets and the fact that 'mini.snippets' uses tree-sitter language name as its context (which is 'tsx' / 'jsx') and not filetype (which is 'typescript' and 'javascript').\r\n\r\nBased on #1637 and [how 'friendly-snippets' organizes its javascript/typescript snippets](https://github.com/rafamadriz/friendly-snippets/tree/main/snippets/javascript), setup similar to something like this should make it work:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal gen_loader = require('mini.snippets').gen_loader\r\nlocal lang_patterns = {\r\n  jsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/react-es7.json' },\r\n  tsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/typescript.json', 'javascript/react-ts.json' },\r\n}\r\nrequire('mini.snippets').setup({\r\n  snippets = {\r\n    gen_loader.from_lang({ lang_patterns = lang_patterns }),\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you want more control over which react snippets to load, adjust `lang_patterns` to include only those files that you want to load for the specific language.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">What setup do you have? If it is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d0464ced00abfd9bbed196fa36ccf3b1691c6b2c/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L379-L390\">this basic recommended one</a> with 'rafamadriz/friendly-snippets' installed then making react snippets to work in tsx/jsx files needs more setup. This is both due to how 'friendly-snippets' organize their snippets and the fact that 'mini.snippets' uses tree-sitter language name as its context (which is 'tsx' / 'jsx') and not filetype (which is 'typescript' and 'javascript').</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Based on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2897443011\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1637\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1637/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1637\">#1637</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/rafamadriz/friendly-snippets/tree/main/snippets/javascript\">how 'friendly-snippets' organizes its javascript/typescript snippets</a>, setup similar to something like this should make it work:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local gen_loader = require('mini.snippets').gen_loader\nlocal lang_patterns = {\n  jsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/react-es7.json' },\n  tsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/typescript.json', 'javascript/react-ts.json' },\n}\nrequire('mini.snippets').setup({\n  snippets = {\n    gen_loader.from_lang({ lang_patterns = lang_patterns }),\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">gen_loader</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.snippets<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_loader</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">lang_patterns</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">jsx</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>javascript/javascript.json<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>javascript/react-es7.json<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">tsx</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>javascript/javascript.json<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>javascript/typescript.json<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>javascript/react-ts.json<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n}\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.snippets<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">snippets</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">gen_loader</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">from_lang</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">lang_patterns</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">lang_patterns</span> }),\n  },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you want more control over which react snippets to load, adjust <code class=\"notranslate\">lang_patterns</code> to include only those files that you want to load for the specific language.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hope this helps.</p>",
            "bodyText": "What setup do you have? If it is this basic recommended one with 'rafamadriz/friendly-snippets' installed then making react snippets to work in tsx/jsx files needs more setup. This is both due to how 'friendly-snippets' organize their snippets and the fact that 'mini.snippets' uses tree-sitter language name as its context (which is 'tsx' / 'jsx') and not filetype (which is 'typescript' and 'javascript').\nBased on #1637 and how 'friendly-snippets' organizes its javascript/typescript snippets, setup similar to something like this should make it work:\nlocal gen_loader = require('mini.snippets').gen_loader\nlocal lang_patterns = {\n  jsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/react-es7.json' },\n  tsx = { 'javascript/javascript.json', 'javascript/typescript.json', 'javascript/react-ts.json' },\n}\nrequire('mini.snippets').setup({\n  snippets = {\n    gen_loader.from_lang({ lang_patterns = lang_patterns }),\n  },\n})\nIf you want more control over which react snippets to load, adjust lang_patterns to include only those files that you want to load for the specific language.\nHope this helps.",
